{"experiments":[  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Patients with high tumor mutational burden (TMB) have shorter overall survival than those with low TMB.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Assess the impact of per‐patient TMB on overall survival using Kaplan‐Meier analysis and log‐rank testing.",  
      "steps":"1. Load cleaned_mutations.csv and cleaned_clinical_data.csv.\n2. Filter mutations to PASS (if FILTER column exists) or include all high‐confidence calls.\n3. Compute TMB per patient as total mutation count per patient_id.\n4. Load clinical data and for each patient define: time = days_to_death if vital_status='Dead', else days_to_last_followup; event = 1 if vital_status='Dead', else 0.\n5. Merge TMB and survival data by patient_id.\n6. Dichotomize TMB at its median into 'High' vs 'Low' groups.\n7. Fit Kaplan‐Meier survival curves for the two groups and perform the log‐rank test.\n8. Plot survival curves with confidence bands and report the log‐rank p‐value.",  
      "deliverables":"• Kaplan‐Meier plot comparing high vs low TMB groups.\n• Table of TMB values, survival times, and event indicators.\n• Log‐rank test statistic and p‐value.\n• Number of patients in each TMB group."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Patients harboring BRAF V600 mutations exhibit higher expression of the MAPK feedback regulator DUSP6.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Test whether the presence of BRAF V600 hotspot mutations is associated with up‐regulation of DUSP6 expression.",  
      "steps":"1. Load cleaned_mutations.csv and identify rows where Hugo_Symbol=='BRAF' and HGVSp_Short contains 'V600'.\n2. Create a patient‐level table with a binary indicator BRAF_V600_status (1=mutant, 0=wild‐type).\n3. Load cleaned_gene_expression.csv, map sample barcodes to patient barcodes (first 12 chars), aggregate to per‐patient mean.\n4. Identify DUSP6 by its Ensembl ID (ENSG00000156908) and extract per‐patient expression.\n5. Merge BRAF_V600_status with DUSP6 expression by patient.\n6. Compare DUSP6 expression between mutant vs wild‐type groups using a Wilcoxon rank‐sum test.\n7. Optionally fit a linear model: DUSP6_expr ~ BRAF_V600_status + age_at_diagnosis + C(gender).",  
      "deliverables":"• Boxplot of DUSP6 expression by BRAF V600 status.\n• Wilcoxon test statistic and p‐value.\n• Table of patient IDs, BRAF_V600_status, and DUSP6 expression.\n• Optional regression coefficients with p‐values."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Patients with TP53 mutations have higher tumor mutational burden compared to TP53 wild‐type patients.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Evaluate whether TP53‐mutant status is associated with elevated per‐patient TMB.",  
      "steps":"1. Load cleaned_mutations.csv and flag patients with at least one mutation in Hugo_Symbol=='TP53'.\n2. Compute TMB per patient as total mutation count.\n3. Create a table of patient_id and TP53_mutant (1/0) and TMB.\n4. Compare TMB distributions between TP53‐mutant and wild‐type groups using a Wilcoxon rank‐sum test.\n5. Report summary statistics (median, IQR) of TMB in each group and test results.",  
      "deliverables":"• Boxplot or violin plot of TMB by TP53 status.\n• Wilcoxon test statistic and p‐value.\n• Table of patient_id, TP53_mutant indicator, and TMB."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Older age at diagnosis is associated with a higher proportion of silent (synonymous) mutations relative to total mutations.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Test whether the silent‐to‐total mutation ratio increases with patient age at diagnosis.",  
      "steps":"1. Load cleaned_mutations.csv and cleaned_clinical_data.csv.\n2. For each patient, count number of mutations with Variant_Classification=='Silent' and total mutations; compute silent_ratio = silent/total.\n3. Merge with clinical data to obtain age_at_diagnosis and gender per patient.\n4. Compute Spearman correlation between age_at_diagnosis and silent_ratio; report rho and p‐value.\n5. Fit linear regression: silent_ratio ~ age_at_diagnosis + C(gender).\n6. Check regression assumptions and report coefficients.",  
      "deliverables":"• Scatter plot of silent_ratio vs age with regression line.\n• Spearman rho and p‐value.\n• Regression summary table: coefficients, R², p‐values.\n• Table of patient_id, age_at_diagnosis, gender, silent_ratio."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Patients with a documented primary melanoma diagnosis (primary_melanoma_dx='YES') have higher tumor mutational burden than those without.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Compare TMB between patients with and without primary melanoma diagnosis.",  
      "steps":"1. Load cleaned_clinical_data.csv and select primary_melanoma_dx status.\n2. Load cleaned_mutations.csv and compute per‐patient TMB.\n3. Merge primary_melanoma_dx with TMB by patient_id.\n4. Filter to patients with non‐missing primary_melanoma_dx.\n5. Compare TMB distributions between 'YES' vs 'NO' using Wilcoxon rank‐sum test.\n6. Summarize medians and IQRs of TMB per group.",  
      "deliverables":"• Boxplot of TMB by primary melanoma diagnosis.\n• Wilcoxon U statistic and p‐value.\n• Table of patient_id, primary_melanoma_dx, and TMB."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Baseline neoplasm status 'WITH TUMOR' is associated with higher tumor proliferation marker MKI67 expression compared to 'TUMOR FREE'.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Assess whether current tumor status correlates with MKI67 expression levels.",  
      "steps":"1. Load cleaned_clinical_data.csv and select baseline_neoplasm_status ('WITH TUMOR' vs 'TUMOR FREE').\n2. Load and aggregate cleaned_gene_expression.csv to per‐patient means.\n3. Extract MKI67 expression (ENSG00000148773) per patient.\n4. Merge neoplasm status with MKI67 expression for patients with non‐missing status and expression.\n5. Compare MKI67 expression between the two groups with a Wilcoxon test.\n6. Optionally adjust for age_at_diagnosis and gender in a linear model: MKI67_expr ~ status + age + C(gender).",  
      "deliverables":"• Violin or boxplot of MKI67 expression by neoplasm status.\n• Wilcoxon test statistic and p‐value.\n• Table of patient_id, baseline_neoplasm_status, and MKI67 expression.\n• Optional regression coefficients and p‐values."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Self‐reported race (White vs Black) is associated with differences in tumor mutational burden in melanoma patients.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Compare per‐patient TMB between self‐identified White and Black or African American patients.",  
      "steps":"1. Load cleaned_clinical_data.csv and filter patients with race=='WHITE' or race=='BLACK OR AFRICAN AMERICAN'.\n2. Load cleaned_mutations.csv and compute TMB per patient.\n3. Merge race information with TMB by patient_id.\n4. Compare TMB between the two racial groups using a Wilcoxon rank‐sum test.\n5. Report group sample sizes and summary statistics.",  
      "deliverables":"• Boxplot of TMB by race (White vs Black).\n• Wilcoxon test statistic and p‐value.\n• Table of patient_id, race, and TMB."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Greater Breslow thickness is positively correlated with expression of the hypoxia‐inducible factor gene HIF1A in tumor samples.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Test the association between Breslow thickness and HIF1A expression as a surrogate for hypoxic adaptation.",  
      "steps":"1. Load cleaned_clinical_data.csv and extract bcr_patient_barcode and breslow_thickness; drop missing values.\n2. Load cleaned_gene_expression.csv, map to patient barcodes, and average per patient.\n3. Identify HIF1A by Ensembl ID ENSG00000100644 and extract per‐patient expression.\n4. Merge Breslow thickness with HIF1A expression by patient.\n5. Compute Spearman correlation between breslow_thickness and HIF1A expression; report rho and p‐value.\n6. Fit linear regression: HIF1A_expr ~ breslow_thickness + age_at_diagnosis + C(gender).\n7. Plot scatter with fitted regression line.",  
      "deliverables":"• Spearman rho and p‐value for Breslow vs HIF1A.\n• Regression summary: coefficients, R², p‐values.\n• Scatter plot with regression line.\n• Table of patient_id, breslow_thickness, and HIF1A expression."  
    }  
  }  
]}
